# THE DEPLOY SERVES THE REPOSITORY, NOT AN APP BUNDLE.
#
# There is no build step here - Cloudflare Pages publishes the repo root as
# the site root. That is what makes a buildless app simple, and it also means
# every file in this repository is a live URL. Verified 2026-09-17:
#
#   /docs/owner-guide/join-qr.png          200, 18 KB  <- a WORKING 500-use
#                                                         join code
#   /docs/owner-guide/pitch-message.txt    200          <- pricing, private
#   /docs/audit/RISK_REGISTER.md           200          <- every boundary and
#                                                         past finding
#   /docs/deploy/PER_CLUB_SETUP.md         200          <- deploy runbook
#   /CHANGES.md, /COMMUNITY_SETUP.md       200
#
# The join QR is the one that is an actual credential rather than a
# disclosure: anyone who fetched that path could scan it and join the club as
# a member. It has to be deactivated in the app, not merely un-published -
# removing the file closes the door, it does not un-ring the bell.
#
# A 404 rather than a redirect: these paths should not exist to a visitor, and
# bouncing them to the app would tell a crawler the directory is real.
#
# ORDER MATTERS. Pages applies the first matching rule, so anything the app
# actually loads must be listed above the blocks. The app loads only
# index.html, the three top-level scripts, /src, /vendor, /assets, the icons
# and the manifest - nothing under any path below.
/docs/*              /404.html  404
/design/*            /404.html  404
/supabase/*          /404.html  404
/test/*              /404.html  404
/scripts/*           /404.html  404
/.github/*           /404.html  404
/*.md                /404.html  404
